@*
    =====================================================================
    VALIDATION SCRIPTS PARTIAL
    Location: MerkaiTrial.Admin.Web/Views/Shared/_ValidationScriptsPartial.cshtml
    (NOTE: the previous header said Pages/Shared/ — it has always lived in
     Views/Shared/. Razor Pages falls back to Views/Shared when resolving a
     partial, which is why it worked despite the wrong comment.)

    Purpose: Client-side validation scripts for forms.

    ── DISABLED 2026-08-01 ──────────────────────────────────────────────
    Both scripts pointed at ~/lib/..., but wwwroot/lib/ does not exist and
    there is no libman.json. They 404'd on every page that includes this
    partial (~25 pages), costing 1.2–3.3s per page load in the Admin.Web
    logs. Client-side validation was therefore NEVER working — this is a
    missing feature, not a regression. Server-side validation is intact
    and is what actually protects the data.

    TO RE-ENABLE properly (do this alongside the real-auth work):
      1. jQuery must be loaded first — check _Layout.cshtml. As of this
         change the layout loads only bootstrap.bundle.min.js, which does
         NOT include jQuery. Uncommenting these lines without adding
         jQuery will throw a JS error instead of a 404.
      2. Then either add libman.json and restore wwwroot/lib/, or switch
         both tags to cdnjs.cloudflare.com — several Admin pages
         (Admin/Roles, Admin/Users, Admin/Tenants) already use cdnjs, so
         that route is consistent with existing practice.
      3. Once wired, the existing [Required] attributes will populate the
         asp-validation-for spans with no further changes.
    ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
